**I think I've found the defect.** Look at `sf32lb_lcd_putarea`:

```c
if ((size_t)stride == row_bytes)
  {
    fb_coord_t y = row_start;
    const fb_coord_t chunk_rows = 24;
    while (y <= row_end) { ... }        /* fast path: 24 rows at a time */
  }
```

There are **two paths**, selected by `stride == row_bytes` — i.e. whether the updated region spans the **full width**. Rect 0 was full-width (`390×2 = 780 = stride`) → fast path → worked. Rects 1–5 were partial-width (`320×2 = 640 ≠ 780`) → the **other** path. Let me read it:

