   **The active thread:** diagnose why the AMOLED panel produces no image. The user explicitly chose **"我再从软件侧攻一轮"** (attack the software side once more).

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - **Board:** 黄山派 = LCKFB Huangshan Pi = SF32LB52-LCHSPI-ULP. Panel: 1.85" 390×450 AMOLED, CO5300 driver, QSPI 4-data-line (QADSPI). Console UART1 @ 1,000,000 8N1, NSH line terminator `\n`.
   - **Flash layout rule (learned the hard way):** `0x12000000` holds the chip's factory bootloader ("FCES", 11,276 bytes) and **must never be overwritten**. The application image goes to **`0x12010000`**.
   - **sftool 0.2.5:** `write_flash <file>@<addr>`, `read_flash <filename@address:size>`; options `-c SF32LB52 -p COM8 -b 1000000 --before default_reset --after soft_reset|no_reset --connect-attempts N --compat true|false`.
   - **CH343 (not CH340N) on COM8.** Neither RTS **nor DTR** is wired to SoC reset — this session tested four DTR/RTS sequences (ESP-style, DTR pulse, RTS pulse, both pulse) and none reset the board. A physical reset (RESET button or USB replug) is the only recovery.
   - **VBoxManage pattern:** binary at `/c/Program Files/Oracle/VirtualBox/VBoxManage.exe`; must `export MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1`; **copyto requires the Windows path form** (`'D:\openvela_setup\x.sh'`), then `guestcontrol openvela-dev run --username openvela --password ***REDACTED*** --exe /bin/bash -- /home/openvela/<script>.sh`, then `copyfrom` back to `D:\openvela_setup\out\`.
   - **WebFetch is blocked for github.com** in this environment ("Unable to verify if domain github.com is safe to fetch"). All GitHub access must go through `curl` inside the VM.
   - **Repo default branch is `dev-ai-contest-2026`** (not `main`/`master`); a stale `master` branch also exists.
   - **Official tutorial pointer** (from our repo's README): `https://github.com/open-vela/docs/blob/dev-ai-contest-2026/zh-cn/contest_2026/ai_hardware/ai_hardware_guide_index.md`. Raw base: `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/open-vela/docs/dev-ai-contest-2026/zh-cn/contest_2026/`.
   - **Compliance mechanism (from README):** 黄山派 is a NuttX "custom board" whose `CONFIG_ARCH_BOARD_CUSTOM_DIR` is a configurable relative path (default `vendor/sifli/boards/sf32lb52/lckfb_huangshan_pi`), so the board defconfig is self-describing — the team added only `board/contest_board/configs/nsh/defconfig` and a `<linkfile>` mapping in the manifest. Manifest maps `app/smart_lock` → `packages/demos/contest2026_296_smart_lock` and `board/contest_board` → `vendor/openvela/boards/contest2026_296_board`.
   - **Build command:** from openvela root: `./build.sh vendor/openvela/boards/contest2026_296_board/configs/nsh --cmake -j$(nproc)` → `cmake_out/contest2026_296_board_nsh/nuttx.bin` (~6.5 MB).
   - **NSH console has no `help <builtin>`** — `help` only knows shell builtins; builtin apps are listed in `help`'s "Builtin Apps:" section.

3. Files and Code Sections:

   - **`D:\openvela_setup\out\fbsrc.txt`** (24,177 bytes) — THE BREAKTHROUGH. Full source of `apps/examples/fb/fb_main.c`, found via `grep -rl "FB test finished"`. Critical excerpts:
